WEBVTT

NOTE English captions for https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fBzrLN77gng, from YouTube, repeats removed.

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:09.240
Then Imam al-Ghazali shares with us various narrations and stories of the pious predecessors.

00:00:09.240 --> 00:00:12.520
Wa Dhul-Qarnain who met an angel

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:16.240
Dhul-Qarnain whose story is mentioned in Surat al-Kahf

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:20.200
he once met one of the angels and he said teach me something

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.400
that will increase my faith and certitude.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.600
And the angel said to him, "Do not become angry

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:29.160
because

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:30.720
the shaytan

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.800
has a greater capability

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:38.880
of controlling the human being when he becomes angered.

00:00:38.880 --> 00:00:45.640
So, respond to anger with by suppressing it.

00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:49.520
And calm the fire of anger

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:54.840
with uh a ta'wuda which is uh being

00:00:54.840 --> 00:01:00.440
the opposite of rushing and being rushed which is deliberation.

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:04.879
And calm the fire of anger with deliberation.

00:01:04.879 --> 00:01:08.560
You know, a lot of times especially when you're young and especially in today's world there's

00:01:08.560 --> 00:01:13.080
so much going on and with social media you have to have an opinion about everything.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:18.560
Everybody is a a commentator and an expert on everything that happens in the world.

00:01:18.560 --> 00:01:23.080
And then particularly people will want to know, you know, "What what what do What does

00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:26.000
Islam have to say about this?"

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:32.440
Often times when things are going on in the world there's current events and things that

00:01:32.440 --> 00:01:36.440
are taking place that are very hot topics.

00:01:36.440 --> 00:01:39.680
The best response is to slow down.

00:01:39.680 --> 00:01:41.840
To really think about it.

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:43.120
Everyone wants to be smart.

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:47.360
Oh, I've got it figured out and I can be the the religious and social commentator

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:48.920
on this.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:51.840
But you might say things that you'll regret later.

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.240
A lot of times just let me think about it.

00:01:54.240 --> 00:02:00.480
A man once asked Imam al-Shafi'i Allah a question and Imam Shafi'i was quiet.

00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:02.760
The man asked again.

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:04.320
And Imam al-Shafi'i said, "Hold on.

00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:12.880
I'm still thinking about whether answering your question or remaining quiet is more beloved to Allah.

00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:16.160
I'm still working on that piece.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:19.000
You know, a man a man came to Imam Malik and asked him all of these

00:02:19.000 --> 00:02:20.640
questions. I don't know.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.040
I don't know. I don't know.

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:23.400
And then he answered a few questions.

00:02:23.400 --> 00:02:25.760
He said, "Man, you don't know?

00:02:25.760 --> 00:02:28.680
You're Imam Malik. Everybody says you know everything."

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:31.960
Imam Malik said, "Go out and tell people I don't know anything.

00:02:31.960 --> 00:02:35.760
It's okay. I'm not here to entertain you.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:38.360
This is This is knowledge of revelation.

00:02:38.360 --> 00:02:39.840
I can't make it up.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:42.320
If I don't know, I have to say I don't know.

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:43.320
I have to think about it.

00:02:43.320 --> 00:02:44.920
I have to research.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:48.240
We have to contemplate, consult.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:50.760
All of these things are so important.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:52.720
And mashallah it's really

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:55.760
very encouraging to see so many young people in the room.

00:02:55.760 --> 00:03:00.440
This is a skill the sooner you you learn it the better.

00:03:00.440 --> 00:03:02.320
Consult people.

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:04.200
Think deeply about things.

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:07.800
Often times your passion is a strength

00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:14.760
but allow that passion and that strength to be guided by deliberation and and seeking advice

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:19.320
from people more experienced and wiser than yourself.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:21.520
Don't be someone who's reactionary.

00:03:21.520 --> 00:03:26.800
There's a difference between taking initiative and being reactionary.

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:30.040
Anger is a very reactionary response.

00:03:30.040 --> 00:03:34.000
So, here the angel is telling Dhul-Qarnain

00:03:34.000 --> 00:03:37.120
calm your anger with deliberation.

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:40.840
Wa iyyaka wal 'ajalah and beware

00:03:40.840 --> 00:03:42.960
of haste.

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:44.400
Rushing.

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.120
Got to do it now.

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.000
Jazakallahu khairan.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:55.600
Fa innaka idha 'ajilta akhta'ta hazzak because if you're hasty you'll make a mistake.

00:03:55.600 --> 00:03:57.000
You'll make a mistake.

00:03:57.000 --> 00:04:03.680
Wa kun sahlan layyinan lil-qaribi wal-ba'id and be easygoing and gentle with people who are close

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:06.240
to you and people who are not close to you.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:11.960
Wa la takun jabbaran 'anida and do not be a

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:18.200
tyrannical person. Someone who is stubborn and obstinate and difficult to be with and who is

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:19.599
harsh with others.
